From b4dc694c94ffa72517be7a38ec88613dbb865ca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:49:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] server: recipient replies: a cut call is the reply's cut
 call, the prompt's open message read, thinking off kept off

A call message max_tokens cuts stays open as far as it was written, named by its header until its invoke names the
tool, so tool_stream reads it as the reply's cut call, whole and streamed, as #1299 made a GLM call; content never
shows its markup. A stop string inside a call keeps the call's text, as the other formats keep theirs. The reply goes
on from the prompt's last unclosed <|start|> header, so a generation prompt that already opened to=self<|message|>
keeps the reasoning after it; Muse Spark Open's template ends at <|start|>assistant, with or without reasoning_effort.
Only calls to offered tools become <tool_call> markup: with no tools, or a tool not offered, a call message stays as
the model wrote it, as DSML, LFM2 and Qwen's XML calls do. Thinking off no longer turns the split's reasoning on: self
messages stay out of the reply, and the template, which has no thinking switch, hears its lowest reasoning effort
rather than its default (xhigh). Raw completion prompts keep the model's text. Tests cut a call before its invoke
names the tool, inside a value, a value's closer, a parameter's name, between parameters, after the invoke closed,
and in a call's header, at strides 1, 3, 7 and whole; and cover an opened prompt, no tools, an unoffered tool and
thinking off.
